        "target": "Given:\n- Cost of the book = $50\n- Mark-up = 30% above cost\n- Discount = 10% during sale\n\nFirst, calculate the marked price:\n\\[ \\text{Marked Price} = \\text{Cost} + (\\text{Cost} \\times \\text{Mark-up}) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Marked Price} = 50 + (50 \\times 0.30) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Marked Price} = 50 + 15 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Marked Price} = 65 \\]\n\nNext, apply the 10% discount to the marked price:\n\\[ \\text{Discounted Price} = \\text{Marked Price} - (\\text{Marked Price} \\times \\text{Discount}) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Discounted Price} = 65 - (65 \\times 0.10) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Discounted Price} = 65 - 6.5 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Discounted Price} = 58.5 \\]\n\nNow, calculate the profit:\n\\[ \\text{Profit} = \\text{Discounted Price} - \\text{Cost} \\]\n\\[ \\text{Profit} = 58.5 - 50 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Profit} = 8.5 \\]\n\nFinally, calculate the percent profit:\n\\[ \\text{Percent Profit} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Profit}}{\\text{Cost}} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Percent Profit} = \\left( \\frac{8.5}{50} \\right) \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Percent Profit} = 0.17 \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Percent Profit} = 17\\% \\]\n\nFINAL: 17",
