        "student_prefix_sha256": "58325b50b942f9d3e5d1830f5cc6979a0035a071014acc1d7293adb055ded120",
        "target": "First, I identify the given quantities:\n- Bobby's salary: $450 per week\n- Federal taxes: 1/3 of $450\n- State taxes: 8% of $450\n- Health insurance: $50 per week\n- Life insurance: $20 per week\n- Parking fee: $10 per week\n\nNext, I calculate the amounts removed:\n1. Federal taxes: \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\times 450 = 150 \\) dollars\n2. State taxes: \\( 0.08 \\times 450 = 36 \\) dollars\n3. Health insurance: $50\n4. Life insurance: $20\n5. Parking fee: $10\n\nNow, I sum up the total deductions:\n- Total deductions: \\( 150 + 36 + 50 + 20 + 10 = 266 \\) dollars\n\nFinally, I subtract the total deductions from Bobby's salary to find the final amount left in his paycheck:\n- Final amount: \\( 450 - 266 = 184 \\) dollars\n\nFINAL: 184",
